diagnostics/operator-method-shape.em:7:10: an operator method takes exactly one parameter
      func times(quantity: Int, extra: Int): Money {
           ^^^^^
The parameter is the value on the right of `*`.
diagnostics/operator-method-shape.em:12:15: an operator parameter cannot have a default
      func less(amount: Int = 1): Money {
                ^^^^^^
An operator always receives its right operand explicitly. Remove the default.
diagnostics/operator-method-shape.em:17:10: an operator method needs an explicit result type
      func split(parts: Int) {
           ^^^^^
Write the result after `:`, as in `func times(quantity: Int): Money`.
